      "topic": "Gas Laws",
      "subtopic": "Boyle's Law",
      "question": "At constant temperature, a gas of volume 600 cm³ at 750 mmHg is compressed to a volume of 450 cm³. Find its new pressure.",
      "options": {
        "A": "1000 mmHg",
        "B": "900 mmHg",
        "C": "850 mmHg",
        "D": "1200 mmHg"
      },
      "answer": "A",
      "explanation": "P2 = (P1 * V1) / V2 = (750 * 600) / 450 = 450000 / 450 = 1000 mmHg.",
      "explanation_short": "P2 = (750 * 600) / 450 = 1000 mmHg.",
      "explanation_pidgin": "Multiply 750 by 600 then divide by 450, you go get 1000 mmHg."
    }
  ]
}
